8. ⟦gN⟧ tokens stand for formatting, locked names, links or kept passages. Only the tokens listed for an item under [Immutable tokens] exist in it: copy each exactly once inside that same item; never translate, drop, add, invent or move one to another item. An item with no listed token holds none.
9. Two tokens around words are a pair: keep both around the translation of those words. A pair never wraps nothing; around one letter (a drop cap) it wraps the first letter of the translated word.
10. A lone token replaces a word, such as a locked name: put it where that word belongs. Other names are plain text (their glossary rendering), never a token. A list-marker token that begins an item stays first. An item of only tokens is copied after its marker.
{{/tokenRules}}
